  "narration": {
    "title": "The Award Races Take Shape at Midseason",
    "intro": "Halfway through the year, the trophies are still up for grabs. The MVP debate runs through Yordan Alvarez's bat, the Cy Young through a Brewers rookie's untouchable line, and the Rookie of the Year through a Japanese slugger on the South Side.",
    "mvp_lead": "Yordan Alvarez tops the elite hitters at 1.069, holding steady week to week on what the data calls a historic pace. Behind him it's a logjam: Ben Rice at .972 and Nick Kurtz at .969, with Kyle Schwarber's 29 homers giving him a different kind of case.",
    "cy_lead": "Jacob Misiorowski is having the kind of season that ends arguments, sitting at a 1.45 ERA and a 0.75 WHIP with the form needle pinned at 100. Cam Schlittler is the closest pursuer at 1.71, his form up to 94, while Cristopher S\u00e1nchez rounds out the chase at 1.80.",
    "roy_lead": "Munetaka Murakami leads the rookie hitters by a wide margin at .938 with 20 homers, comfortably the class of the group. Bryce Eldridge follows at .874, and Travis Bazzana is making a late push, his OPS up 56 points to .803."
  }
